        {
          "comment": "Every foundry VIA1 keeps M1 0.005 um past the cut on all sides, which on a 0.09 um tall cell pin lands 0.085 um from the cell's own M1 (rule: 0.09), so many pins had no access point. The design rules (VIAn-En.2a/2b) allow 0 on two sides when the other two have 0.04; add those vias.",
